  "method": "Use source-exact quarter-turn integer affine transforms to normalize the two bracket rectangles and one insert rectangle by their bounding-box minimum. All12 allowed orientations are represented by10 exactly equivalent normalized classes. Reconstruct fixed original polygons, form zero-clearance Minkowski obstacles for each normalized class, and expand their union by the verified circumscribed128-gon with clearance0.22 plus0.0001mm numerical margin. Subtract this from inward stock anchor domains with0.02mm additional margin. Constrained triangulation exactly covers each safe region; merge only exactly convex adjacent unions. Merge caps preserve all unmerged faces. Encode each CCW face edge with exact rational coefficients from its stored binary-float vertices. Round a,b times10^7 to integers, subtract the exact worst-case coefficient error over positive bounded grid coordinates plus one unit, and floor the bound. Every admitted0.01mm-grid point therefore lies inside that safe convex face. This is a conservative feasible-subset construction, not a continuous outer relaxation or unrestricted impossibility test.",
  "limits": "One120-second geometry phase, with no new query after its deadline. Preserve pending queries, cap-hit unmerged faces and all failures; do not extend or rerun. No solver runs in this script. A later model is allowed only after independent geometry/rounding verification and model field checks; one60-second eight-worker seed-zero solve is declared here.",
